      "group_size": 4,
      "text": "Adomnán sang [this]."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "celt/spruch-adamnans#SprAdamn.1",
      "source_sha256": "90d9be0b8bbce89b",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-12",
      "group_size": 4,
      "text": "Three certain steps for everyone, the best that anyone will take until Doomsday: a step to visit a sick person at his dwelling [?], a step of pilgrimage, a step to church."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "celt/spruch-adamnans#SprAdamn.2",
      "source_sha256": "8f003460e82d2f26",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-12",
      "group_size": 4,
      "text": "If one goes to a servant of God (a Céle Dé), he eats and moves about along with him; everything that he does in the cell where he is would be good in everyone's eyes [?]."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "celt/spruch-adamnans#SprAdamn.3",
      "source_sha256": "2bf1372d923b771c",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-12",
      "group_size": 4,
      "text": "Woe to him who is on the path of danger, and woe to him who is reared without a rule. It is time to give up follies: people do not go in order of their age."
    }
  ]
}
